                <pb facs="0837" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg717"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12 Gomez and Rubio/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-25T14:00:00-04:00">June 25, 1931—2
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>183. Your 213, June 23, 1 p.m. The Department was informed this; morning by
                    telephone from the Governor of Oklahoma that the expenses of Salvador Cortés
                    Rubio would be fully taken care of.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
